{"header":{"type":"esummary","version":"0.3"},"result":{"uids":["200349270","200349221"],"200349270":{"uid":"200349270","accession":"GSE349270","gds":"","title":"Cytoplasmic RBM20 granules are sufficient to drive severe dilated cardiomyopathy","summary":"Pathogenic genetic variants in the RBM20 gene, encoding the splicing factor RNA binding motif protein 20 (RBM20), are causative in a severe form of dilated cardiomyopathy (DCM) known as RBM20 cardiomyopathy.Certain variants in RBM20 disrupt a nuclear localization signal (NLS) in the protein, impairing nuclear import and leading to its accumulation in cytoplasmic granules.We recently showed that non-targeted knockdown of RBM20 improves cardiac function in mice heterozygous for an NLS-disrupting Rbm20 variant secondary to alleviation of cytoplasmic RBM20 granule burden. Notably, the improvement in cardiac function occurred despite similar or worsened mis-splicing of RBM20 target genes.These findings strongly support a role for cytoplasmic RBM20 granules in disease severity; yet it is not clear whether these molecular assemblies can drive the development of severe DCM. The findings of the present study directly demonstrate that cytoplasmic RBM20 granules cause severe DCM in mice with minimal contributions from target gene mis-splicing.","gpl":"34290","gse":"349270","taxon":"Mus musculus","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2026/10/05","suppfile":"TSV","samples":[{"accession":"GSM10090449","title":"R26-Het; Cre-WT_S389"},{"accession":"GSM10090452","title":"R26-Het; Cre-WT_S427"},{"accession":"GSM10090446","title":"R26-WT; Cre-KI_S425"},{"accession":"GSM10090458","title":"R26-Het; Cre-KI_S401"},{"accession":"GSM10090435","title":"R26-WT; Cre-WT_S388"},{"accession":"GSM10090455","title":"R26-Het; Cre-KI_S397"},{"accession":"GSM10090438","title":"R26-WT; Cre-WT_S418"},{"accession":"GSM10090457","title":"R26-Het; Cre-KI_S400"},{"accession":"GSM10090451","title":"R26-Het; Cre-WT_S414"},{"accession":"GSM10090454","title":"R26-Het; Cre-KI_S391"},{"accession":"GSM10090440","title":"R26-WT; Cre-WT_S421"},{"accession":"GSM10090443","title":"R26-WT; Cre-KI_S406"},{"accession":"GSM10090437","title":"R26-WT; Cre-WT_S396"},{"accession":"GSM10090439","title":"R26-WT; Cre-WT_S420"},{"accession":"GSM10090456","title":"R26-Het; Cre-KI_S398"},{"accession":"GSM10090436","title":"R26-WT; Cre-WT_S394"},{"accession":"GSM10090448","title":"R26-Het; Cre-WT_S392"},{"accession":"GSM10090442","title":"R26-WT; Cre-KI_S399"},{"accession":"GSM10090445","title":"R26-WT; Cre-KI_S422"},{"accession":"GSM10090441","title":"R26-WT; Cre-KI_S393"},{"accession":"GSM10090444","title":"R26-WT; Cre-KI_S419"},{"accession":"GSM10090453","title":"R26-Het; Cre-KI_S390"},{"accession":"GSM10090450","title":"R26-Het; Cre-WT_S395"},{"accession":"GSM10090447","title":"R26-Het; Cre-WT_S385"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":24,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":[],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE349nnn/GSE349270/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA1537677"},"200349221":{"uid":"200349221","accession":"GSE349221","gds":"","title":"RNA-sequencing of JMJD5 (KDM8) knock-out and wild-type HepG2 cells","summary":"JMJD5 (KDM8) is a 2-oxoglutarate-dependent oxygenase that hydroxylates the splicing factor ISY1 and, through it, regulates the arginine methyltransferase PRMT6. To establish which of the proteomic changes caused by loss of JMJD5 are reflected at the transcript level, we sequenced poly-A selected RNA from wild-type HepG2 cells and from an isogenic CRISPR/Cas9 JMJD5 knock-out, four biological replicates per genotype. The methionine and one-carbon programme, including BHMT and BHMT2, is induced at the transcript level, whereas the majority of JMJD5-dependent proteome changes are not mirrored in the transcriptome. The knock-out was generated with two guide RNAs targeting a single coding exon; the sequencing shows the expected excision between the two protospacers while total KDM8 mRNA is essentially unchanged, consistent with loss of the protein but retention of a stable transcript.","gpl":"30173","gse":"349221","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2026/10/05","suppfile":"TSV","samples":[{"accession":"GSM10089534","title":"HepG2 wild-type, biological replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM10089537","title":"HepG2 JMJD5 (KDM8) knock-out, biological replicate 1"},{"accession":"GSM10089540","title":"HepG2 JMJD5 (KDM8) knock-out, biological replicate 4"},{"accession":"GSM10089539","title":"HepG2 JMJD5 (KDM8) knock-out, biological replicate 3"},{"accession":"GSM10089536","title":"HepG2 wild-type, biological replicate 4"},{"accession":"GSM10089533","title":"HepG2 wild-type, biological replicate 1"},{"accession":"GSM10089538","title":"HepG2 JMJD5 (KDM8) knock-out, biological replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM10089535","title":"HepG2 wild-type, biological replicate 3"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":8,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":[],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE349nnn/GSE349221/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA1537591"}}}
